{"id":"edit-distance","title":"Edit distance","difficulty":"medium","pattern":"two-sequence DP","statement":"<p>Return the minimum number of single-character insertions, deletions and substitutions turning a into b.</p>","entry":{"python":"min_distance","cpp":{"name":"minDistance","ret":"int","params":[["string","a"],["string","b"]]}},"kind":"function","compare":"exact","time_limit_ms":2000,"hints":["dp[i][j] = the distance between a[:i] and b[:j]; base cases dp[i][0] = i, dp[0][j] = j.","Last characters equal: dp[i\u22121][j\u22121]. Else 1 + min(substitute, delete, insert)."],"complexity":"O(|a|\u00b7|b|)","starter":{"python":"def min_distance(a, b):\n    pass\n","cpp":"int minDistance(string a, string b) {\n    \n}\n"},"tests":[{"args":["horse","ros"],"expected":3,"sample":true},{"args":["intention","execution"],"expected":5,"sample":true},{"args":["","abc"],"expected":3},{"args":["abc",""],"expected":3},{"args":["kitten","sitting"],"expected":3},{"args":["",""],"expected":608},{"args":["",""],"expected":296}],"solution":{"explanation":"<p>Each of the three operations corresponds to one neighbour in the table: substitute \u2196, delete \u2191, insert \u2190. The base row and column encode \"transform into or from the empty string\". Edit distance is everywhere in practice: diff tools, spell checkers, DNA alignment (with different costs), and the compiler course's tree matching.</p>","python":"def min_distance(a, b):\n    prev = list(range(len(b) + 1))\n    for i, x in enumerate(a, 1):\n        cur = [i]\n        for j, y in enumerate(b, 1):\n            cur.append(prev[j - 1] if x == y else 1 + min(prev[j - 1], prev[j], cur[j - 1]))\n        prev = cur\n    return prev[-1]\n","cpp":"int minDistance(string a, string b) {\n    int m = b.size(); vector<int> prev(m + 1), cur(m + 1); iota(prev.begin(), prev.end(), 0);\n    for (size_t i = 1; i <= a.size(); i++) { cur[0] = i; for (int j = 1; j <= m; j++) cur[j] = a[i-1] == b[j-1] ? prev[j-1] : 1 + min({prev[j-1], prev[j], cur[j-1]}); swap(prev, cur); }\n    return prev[m];\n}\n"}}